DESCRIPTION >
    Compacts activities from same issue into one, keeping necessary information in a single row. Helps to serve issue-wide widgets in the development tab.
    Opened and closed events are unfiltered, so issues opened or closed by bots (e.g. stale bots) are included, the same way
    `pull_requests_analyzed` includes bot activity. Issues are still limited to enabled repositories, matching the cleaned buckets.
    The unfiltered buckets are refreshed once a day, so the opened and closed events also include the realtime MV
    (`activityRelations_enrich_snapshot_MV_ds`), which holds the last few days of activity changes, including the ones the daily
    bucket merge has not taken in yet. This keeps issues as fresh as the hourly cleaned buckets. The MV is read whole: looking up
    each bucket's latest snapshot scans the bucket datasources and is too slow for the push-time check.
    The first non-author response still comes from the bot-filtered `activityRelations_deduplicated_cleaned_bucket_union`, so an
    automated bot comment does not count as a response.
    The unfiltered buckets are read once per run: `issue_events` reads both event types together, and `issues` is referenced
    only by the final node. A node referenced twice is computed twice, and reading the buckets takes most of the run.

NODE issue_events_delta
DESCRIPTION >
    Issue opened and closed events from the realtime MV, keeping the most recently updated version of each activity.

SQL >
    SELECT
        activityId,
        sourceId,
        sourceParentId,
        timestamp,
        segmentId,
        channel,
        platform,
        memberId,
        organizationId,
        type
    FROM activityRelations_enrich_snapshot_MV_ds
    WHERE type IN ('issues-opened', 'issues-closed')
    ORDER BY updatedAt DESC
    LIMIT 1 BY segmentId, timestamp, type, platform, channel, sourceId

NODE issue_events
DESCRIPTION >
    Issue opened and closed events from the daily unfiltered buckets and the MV, in one read of the buckets. An opened event
    that also appears in the MV is replaced by its MV version. A close keeps both versions, since only the earliest close per
    issue is used.

SQL >
    SELECT
        activityId,
        sourceId,
        sourceParentId,
        timestamp,
        segmentId,
        channel,
        platform,
        memberId,
        organizationId,
        type
    FROM activityRelations_enriched_deduplicated_bucket_union
    WHERE
        type IN ('issues-opened', 'issues-closed')
        AND (
            type = 'issues-closed'
            OR activityId
            NOT IN (SELECT activityId FROM issue_events_delta WHERE type = 'issues-opened')
        )
    UNION ALL
    SELECT
        activityId,
        sourceId,
        sourceParentId,
        timestamp,
        segmentId,
        channel,
        platform,
        memberId,
        organizationId,
        type
    FROM issue_events_delta

NODE issues
DESCRIPTION >
    One row per issue opened in an enabled repository, with the issue's first close from any repository. Opened events key
    on `sourceId` and closes on `sourceParentId`, so grouping by that key pairs them without a join. `openerCount` is the
    number of distinct non-empty openers per issue and `soleOpener` is the opener when there is one, for the response rule in
    the final node.

SQL >
    SELECT
        tupleElement(opened, 1) AS id,
        tupleElement(opened, 2) AS sourceId,
        tupleElement(opened, 3) AS openedAt,
        tupleElement(opened, 4) AS segmentId,
        tupleElement(opened, 5) AS channel,
        tupleElement(opened, 6) AS platform,
        tupleElement(opened, 7) AS memberId,
        tupleElement(opened, 8) AS organizationId,
        firstClosedAt,
        openerCount,
        soleOpener
    FROM
        (
            SELECT arrayJoin(openedRows) AS opened, firstClosedAt, openerCount, soleOpener
            FROM
                (
                    SELECT
                        if(type = 'issues-opened', sourceId, sourceParentId) AS issueKey,
                        minIf(
                            timestamp, type = 'issues-closed' AND sourceParentId != ''
                        ) AS firstClosedAt,
                        uniqExactIf(memberId, isOpened AND memberId != '') AS openerCount,
                        anyIf(memberId, isOpened AND memberId != '') AS soleOpener,
                        groupArrayIf(
                            (
                                activityId,
                                sourceId,
                                timestamp,
                                segmentId,
                                lower(channel),
                                platform,
                                memberId,
                                organizationId
                            ),
                            isOpened
                        ) AS openedRows
                    FROM
                        (
                            SELECT
                                *,
                                type = 'issues-opened'
                                AND (
                                    (
                                        platform IN ('git', 'gerrit', 'github', 'gitlab')
                                        AND (lower(channel), segmentId)
                                        IN (SELECT lower(channel), segmentId FROM repos_to_channels)
                                    )
                                    OR platform NOT IN ('git', 'gerrit', 'github', 'gitlab')
                                ) AS isOpened
                            FROM issue_events
                            WHERE toYear(timestamp) >= 1971
                        )
                    GROUP BY issueKey
                )
        )

NODE issue_first_commenters
DESCRIPTION >
    The first two distinct commenters per issue from the bot-filtered buckets, sorted by each one's first comment. The first
    non-author response is the first commenter's comment, or the second's when the first is the opener.

SQL >
    SELECT
        sourceParentId,
        tupleElement(firstTwo[1], 1) AS firstCommentAt,
        tupleElement(firstTwo[1], 2) AS firstCommenterId,
        if(length(firstTwo) > 1, tupleElement(firstTwo[2], 1), NULL) AS secondCommentAt
    FROM
        (
            SELECT sourceParentId, groupArraySorted(2)((firstCommentAt, memberId)) AS firstTwo
            FROM
                (
                    SELECT sourceParentId, memberId, MIN(timestamp) AS firstCommentAt
                    FROM activityRelations_deduplicated_cleaned_bucket_union
                    WHERE
                        type = 'issue-comment'
                        AND sourceParentId != ''
                        AND memberId != ''
                        AND toYear(timestamp) >= 1971
                    GROUP BY sourceParentId, memberId
                )
            GROUP BY sourceParentId
        )

NODE issue_analysis_results_merged
DESCRIPTION >
    A response comes from someone other than the opener. When an issue has two or more distinct openers, every commenter
    differs from one of them, so the first comment counts.

SQL >
    SELECT
        i.id,
        i.sourceId,
        i.segmentId as segmentId,
        i.channel,
        i.platform,
        i.memberId,
        i.organizationId,
        i.openedAt,
        multiIf(
            i.openerCount = 0 OR c.sourceParentId = '',
            NULL,
            i.openerCount > 1 OR c.firstCommenterId != i.soleOpener,
            c.firstCommentAt,
            c.secondCommentAt
        ) AS commentedAt,
        IF(i.firstClosedAt = toDateTime(0), NULL, i.firstClosedAt) AS closedAt,
        IF(
            closedAt IS NULL,
            NULL,
            toUnixTimestamp(toDateTime(i.firstClosedAt)) - toUnixTimestamp(toDateTime(i.openedAt))
        ) AS closedInSeconds,
        IF(
            commentedAt IS NULL,
            NULL,
            toUnixTimestamp(toDateTime(commentedAt)) - toUnixTimestamp(toDateTime(i.openedAt))
        ) AS respondedInSeconds
    FROM issues i
    LEFT JOIN issue_first_commenters c ON i.sourceId = c.sourceParentId

TYPE COPY
TARGET_DATASOURCE issues_analyzed
COPY_MODE replace
COPY_SCHEDULE 20 * * * *
